B.bB2=new A.tL("none","Nothing happens: the device gets no power.",!1,!1,!1)
B.bB3=new A.tL("none","It cannot be judged: the wire functions were not verified.",!1,!1,!1)
B.bB4=new A.tL("smoke","The loose connection overheats: it glows, smokes and chars the device. In a real wall this can start a fire.",!1,!1,!0)
B.bB5=new A.tL("none","It does not work as it should: some part runs wrongly or not at all. That does not tell you what is wrong, so check against the diagram.",!1,!1,!1)
B.bB6=new A.tL("none","It runs. There is nothing to see, and that is the danger: with no ground, a fault would energize the metal parts.",!0,!1,!1)
B.bB7=new A.tL("none","It works as the diagram says.",!0,!1,!1)
B.bB8=new A.tL("none","It works, and every safety rule is met.",!0,!1,!1)
B.bB9=new A.tL("none","Nothing happens: it is dead. But the hot wire is connected, so it can still be live. No sparks, no smoke: that does not make it safe.",!1,!1,!1)
B.bBa=new A.tL("spark","Bare copper touches something it should not: sparks. The circuit is not safe.",!1,!1,!1)
B.bBb=new A.tL("none","It looks fine for now. But the support cannot carry the weight, and it can fall later.",!1,!1,!1)
B.bBc=new A.tL("fire","BANG. A short circuit: a flash, sparks, smoke and a flame at the device. The breaker trips and the device is ruined. The wires and the device are not safe to use.",!1,!0,!0)
B.bBd=new A.tL("arc","Hot and neutral are reversed: the parts that should be dead are live. Blue arcs show the energized metal. The simulator does not let anything run on this: it is unsafe, even if a real appliance might seem to work.",!1,!1,!1)
B.bBe=new A.tL("arc","Current flows through the ground wire and the metal parts it joins. Arcs crackle at the box. This is a shock hazard.",!1,!1,!1)
B.bBf=new A.tL("spark","The neutral and ground are joined: the protective device trips with a snap of sparks.",!1,!0,!1)
