B.ca5=new A.k9("Breaker off, then test","Before you touch any wire, switch its breaker OFF, then check with a voltage tester that the wire is dead. A switch on the wall is not enough.")
B.c9T=new A.k9("Lock out, tag out","On a real job you put a lock or a note on the panel so nobody switches the power back on while you work.")
B.cac=new A.k9("Water and power","Water carries electricity. Near sinks, tubs and outdoors the outlets must be GFCI, and wet hands never touch wires.")
B.c9Y=new A.k9("Eyes, ears, lungs","Safety glasses for drilling and cutting, ear protection for loud tools, and a mask when you sand drywall dust or cut tile.")
B.cab=new A.k9("Shut the water off","Before you cut or loosen a pipe, close the main water valve and open a faucet to drain the line.")
B.dxG=w([B.ca5,B.c9T,B.cac,B.c9Y,B.cab],x.e)
B.cao=new A.NW("Safety first","\ud83e\uddba",D.c0,B.dxG)
B.cad=new A.k9("Wire colours","Black is hot (it carries the power), white is neutral (the way back), bare copper or green is ground (the safety path). Red is a second hot, often used for a switched line.")
B.cak=new A.k9("Screw colours","On an outlet the brass screw takes the hot wire, the silver screw takes the neutral and the green screw takes the ground.")
B.ca7=new A.k9("Wire size","14 gauge wire is for 15 amp circuits (lights and outlets). 12 gauge is for 20 amp circuits (kitchens). A thinner wire than the breaker allows can overheat and start a fire.")
B.ca1=new A.k9("Breakers","A breaker is a safety switch. It trips when a circuit carries too much current, so the wires never get hot enough to burn.")
B.caf=new A.k9("Wire nuts","Strip about 3/4 inch, twist the bare ends together clockwise, and screw on the nut until no bare copper shows. Give each wire a gentle tug.")
B.cal=new A.k9("Switches","A switch cuts the hot wire only. The neutral goes straight through to the light.")
B.cam=new A.k9("GFCI","A GFCI outlet watches the current going out and coming back. If a little leaks (through water or a person) it cuts the power in a fraction of a second.")
B.c9V=new A.k9("Ceiling fans","A fan shakes and is heavy. It needs a box that says fan rated, fixed to the joist, not a plain light box.")
B.c9X=new A.k9("Heights","Outlets sit about 16 inches from the floor. Switches sit about 48 inches up, where your hand falls.")
B.dp4=w([B.cad,B.cak,B.ca7,B.ca1,B.caf,B.cal,B.cam,B.c9V,B.c9X],x.e)
B.car=new A.NW("Wiring basics","\u26a1",D.bu,B.dp4)
B.c9U=new A.k9("Hot left, cold right","On a faucet, hot is on the left and cold on the right. Hot lines are marked red and cold lines blue.")
B.ca6=new A.k9("The P-trap","The curved pipe under a sink always holds a little water. That water seal stops sewer gas coming up the drain.")
B.cah=new A.k9("Shut-off valves","Every sink and toilet has its own small valve, so you can stop the water to one fixture without turning off the whole house.")
B.ca_=new A.k9("Slip nuts","Drain joints are sealed by a washer and a slip nut. Tighten by hand and a quarter turn: too much force cracks plastic.")
B.c9Z=new A.k9("Wax ring","A toilet sits on a wax ring that seals it to the floor drain. A toilet is lowered straight down once, and cannot be slid around.")
B.cae=new A.k9("Drain slope","Drains fall about 1/4 inch per foot so water and waste keep moving. Too flat and it clogs, too steep and the water leaves the solids behind.")
B.caj=new A.k9("Order of work","Plumbing goes from the top down on the drain (tailpiece, trap, arm) and from the wall out on the supply (valve, hose, fixture).")
B.csF=w([B.c9U,B.ca6,B.cah,B.ca_,B.c9Z,B.cae,B.caj],x.e)
B.cap=new A.NW("Plumbing basics","\ud83d\udeb0",D.cw,B.csF)
B.c9W=new A.k9("Studs","Studs are the vertical 2x4 posts inside a wall, 16 inches apart from centre to centre. Everything is fixed to them.")
B.ca9=new A.k9("Drilling studs","Holes for cable go through the middle of the stud, so a nail or screw cannot reach the wire.")
B.ca0=new A.k9("Drywall","A sheet is 4 feet wide, so its edges land on studs 48 inches apart. Screws go into studs only, just under the paper.")
B.ca3=new A.k9("Taping and mud","Seams get paper tape and three thin coats of joint compound, sanded smooth between coats, then primer and paint.")
B.cai=new A.k9("Order of a build","Frame, run the pipes and wires (rough-in), inspect, hang drywall, finish it, paint, then fit the fixtures and devices.")
B.d7M=w([B.c9W,B.ca9,B.ca0,B.ca3,B.cai],x.e)
B.can=new A.NW("Framing and walls","\ud83c\udfe0",D.ee,B.d7M)
B.ca4=new A.k9("Voltage tester","A pen that glows or beeps near live wires. Test it on a known live outlet first, so you know it works.")
B.caa=new A.k9("Wire strippers","Strip the plastic off without nicking the copper. A nick weakens the wire.")
B.cag=new A.k9("Adjustable wrench","For nuts on valves and hoses. Hold the fitting steady with a second wrench so you do not twist the pipe.")
B.ca8=new A.k9("Drill and screw gun","A drill makes holes through studs. A screw gun sets drywall screws to the right depth.")
B.ca2=new A.k9("Level and tape measure","Measure twice, cut once. A level makes sure outlets, shelves and pipes are straight.")
